# Academy scheduling first (reference UX)

Finish the **academy scheduling experience** first and treat it as the reference UX. Do **not** immediately force trainer parity for every academy UI change.

After academy scheduling is stable, run a **trainer parity audit** and copy/adapt the academy reference experience.

## Before each academy scheduling change

1. Classify the work: **UX** vs **business logic**.
2. Implement accordingly (see below).
3. Do not refactor trainer pages to match academy layout unless explicitly requested.

## Academy-only for now (UX / layout)

May stay under academy routes and academy-specific components until the parity audit:

- Dashboard layout
- Onboarding
- Academy calendar layout (tabs, list view, filters, deep links)
- Academy list/table UX
- Academy settings UI
- Academy public profile logic

Paths/examples: `src/pages/academy/**`, academy-specific layout in `src/components/academy/**` when purely presentational.

## Shared business logic (extract now)

Must live in **`src/lib/`**, shared hooks, or shared components used by both surfaces when the rule is domain logic—not academy chrome.

Includes:

- Pricing calculation (`bookingPricing`, `pricing`, VAT display mapping)
- Split payment calculation and rebalance rules
- Booking insert rules and validation helpers
- Guest player loading patterns (when not layout-specific)
- Invoice creation/update logic (`invoiceAfterAddPlayer`, `affectedInvoices`, `invoiceUpdateChoice`, `applyAffectedInvoiceUpdates`, `invoiceSync` recalc policy)
- Paid status aggregation (`cyclusGroupPayment`, calendar paid filters)
- Cycle/group filtering helpers
- RLS-sensitive query builders

Trainer UI may keep its own layout but should **import** these helpers later—not duplicate formulas or invoice policy.

## Shared trainer components (reuse, not parity)

Components under `src/components/trainer/` that implement **domain flows** (e.g. `InlineBookPlayer`, `BookForPlayerDialog`) are acceptable shared surfaces when they encode business rules via `src/lib`. Academy may import them or wrap them; do not block academy work to restyle trainer first.

## Invoice / booking policy (unchanged)

- Draft invoices: auto-update.
- Sent/pending/overdue: explicit admin confirmation before update.
- Paid: never auto-update.
- Cancelled: ignore.
- €0 bookings: no invoice creation.

## Anti-patterns

- Copying academy calendar JSX into trainer pages “for parity” during an academy fix.
- Duplicating pricing or invoice logic inside `src/pages/academy/**` handlers.
- Changing trainer-only layout to match academy in the same PR as an academy UX tweak.

## Trainer parity audit (later)

When scheduled: compare academy reference flows to trainer calendar/slot detail; migrate UI using existing `src/lib` helpers; document gaps in a short audit note.
